# Decided
- trueqbit (35): every node header carries Purpose and Intention in its
  @file block, also one defining a single node: a node header groups a node
  family - the node structs, their factories, the trait definitions - and
  the Purpose is as wide as the family; more headers were weighed and
  rejected. A brief doc-comment goes on the nodes themselves where the
  name leaves them open (a commit of its own; schema/ nodes in the schema/
  pass); the rule goes into vocabulary-layer.md "Adding a new DSL node" in
  a commit of its own.
- The node headers share one Intention: "a node header of `ast/`, placed by
  source-layout.md; specializes the vocabulary axes in place, as
  vocabulary-layer.md holds, and is gathered by node_definitions.h". The
  reviewer checked each claim against the tree. operand_tags.h and
  crud/set_definitions.h, which are no node headers, carry their own.
- trueqbit (2): assign_t is a binary operator with a grammar trait and stays
  in operators.h; the grammar trait exists to decouple it from crud/. The
  Purpose names no member: "represent the unary and binary operators on
  expressions."
- trueqbit (1): rowid.h's Purpose drops "under each of its three names,
  unqualified or qualified by a table" - the struct names say it. Its file
  comment is cut down to its one why, placed above the qualified nodes.
- trueqbit (34): app_function.h is no split candidate - the UDF traits and
  callable_arguments are what a definition is made of. Purpose: "represent
  an application-defined function: the definition that generates its calls,
  and the calls."
- trueqbit (33): VALUES as an operand of IN is SQLite grammar (a VALUES
  clause is a select-core); values.h's Note stands. sqlite_orm lacks the
  spelling, which goes to TODO.md in its own commit; TODO items go to
  TODO.md alone, not the ledger.
- Claude, from the reviewer: result_columns.h "beyond a bare expression"
  (as_optional wraps a single expression); app_function.h "the traits this
  header declares"; set_definitions.h names set.h in the Intention only.
  get_all_t's result_type versus return_type is left to the two aliases.

